O.K., you asked for it. For those of you who haven't read "The Colour of Magic",
*****SPOILER*****

The main running joke in the first hubworld book is Twoflower, the Hub's first
tourist - he behaves  much like a hack tourist right down to the Hawaian shirt
and camera - but his big trump card is a chest made of "sentient pearwood",
referred to universally as "The luggage". This has several properties; a) It
can contain just about anything, from laundry to gold - each time you open it
it's got something different in there: b) It's intensely loyal, following it's
master to the ends of the earth (and in fact in the book, even beyond...), and
also highly dangerous (it's got teeth in there, and it can easily swallow 
someone whole... nobody knows where they go, but it's not here.... c) it follows
you around on lots and lots and lots of little legs...

	What I thought of in game terms is a cort of mongrel of the dog, the 
Archeologist's frig' and a fountain... You meet it down the dungeon, tame it 
(by throwing it a magic item.... ???) and then it will follow you around dog-like,
fighting for you etc. If you open it (mechanism? search me - add a #open command
I guess) there will be a random thing/things in there....

That's my suggestion. Might be an idea  to have the suitable sound effects
too (see the book to see what I mean). Which reminds me: have Terry Pratchett's
books come out in the 'States yet? If and when you can get them I would give
them a No. 1 reccomendation. Imagine a Fafhrd + Grey Mouser book written by
Douglas Adams, and you'll get the idea. The books are still coming out in
